# App Review demo account for scripts/review_account.sh (skill heji-review-account). Sourced as bash.
# The password is never here: it lives in ~/Credentials/review-accounts.env and App Store Connect.

REVIEW_EMAIL="appreview+tradeboard@hejitech.com"
# The Worker that serves POST /api/review-sign-in, and where it runs.
WORKER_DIR="projects/tradeboard/services/web"
WRANGLER_ENV="production"
SITE="https://tradeboard.hejitech.workers.dev"
BUNDLE_ID="com.hejitech.tradeboard"
# The portal API refuses writes without this header, and answers a sign-in with its own cookie.
SIGNIN_HEADER="X-Tradeboard: 1"
SIGNIN_OK='"signed_in":true'

# App Store Connect › App Review Information › Notes.
REVIEW_NOTES="Sign in: on the first screen tap \"Sign in with email\" (below Continue with Apple) and use the demo account above. People create accounts with Sign in with Apple and a two-factor code from an authenticator app; email sign-in is only for accounts we hand out, such as this one, and skips the two-factor step.

Tradeboard is the iPhone companion of Trading Plan Board. AI agents the user connects over MCP draft and debate trade plans on the user's private board; only the user approves them. Orders are placed only by an executor program the user runs on their own computer through their own brokerage connection: this app never places orders and never sees brokerage credentials.

Each sign-in with the demo account starts from a demo board in dry-run mode with no executor connected, so nothing can trade: a DEMO plan ready for approval (open it, read the ticket, thesis and agent discussion, then Approve or Reject), a DEMO plan still under discussion with an open agent question, and a walkthrough DEMO plan. Settings shows the strategy, the safety policy and connected hosts (none for this account).

Account deletion: Settings > Delete My Board deletes the board and everything on it (plans, history, policy, strategy, agents, executor credentials) and signs out. The same Apple sign-in also opens our other apps, so their data isn't touched."
